+# Offline execution adaptation: upstream, this call queries the figshare data
+# repository API over the network to learn the article's file names and md5
+# checksums for doi:10.6084/m9.figshare.22716739.v1. The reference environment
+# is offline, so the identical registry (one '<name> md5:<provider_md5>' line
+# per dataset file, built from that same provider metadata) is written into the
+# cache by the input-staging recipe and loaded from disk here. Only that
+# ambient network access is removed: pooch still resolves each cached file
+# and checks its md5 against this registry before sc.read_10x_h5 reads it, so
+# the dataset bytes the analysis sees are the original provider files.
